Kodi VAAPI zero-reference Bob compatibility patch
Base: xbmc/xbmc a3a448d26b8d560a65655dab2cd122994dc4e146 (21.3-Omega)
Source: https://github.com/xbmc/xbmc/tree/a3a448d26b8d560a65655dab2cd122994dc4e146
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, as in the modified Kodi source files; retain their notices.

This patch is not applied or installed by CrystalHD. Rebuild Kodi locally after
applying it to the stated baseline. A full patched Kodi build is not qualified here.
It preserves genuine VPP reference requirements and uses the previous successful
source PTS interval only when a zero-reference Bob second output lacks ptsLast.
The first unknown interval is unchanged; this is not a general VFR-duration proof.
Bob alone reports synchronous postprocessing to avoid prioritizing its blocking
Filter over queued output; other postprocessing methods keep the existing policy.

From a clean checkout of the exact Kodi baseline:
  git apply --check /path/to/kodi-vaapi-bob.patch
  git apply /path/to/kodi-vaapi-bob.patch

